-- title:
--   Kernel of the Tate-point classifying map lies in every prime power
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q \ge 5$ and $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \neq q$, and a nonzero natural number $M'$ divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero carrying a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity $\xi$ for which some ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ attached to [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$, and let $j \in K$ be a nonzero element whose Laurent expansion is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the rational $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal $(q)$, acting on $K$ and on $A$ compatibly, such that $A$ is a module-finite $A_0$-algebra generated by a single element $\zeta_A$ whose image in $L$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity, such that $\ell$ and $M'$ are invertible in $A_0$ and $A_0$ contains a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity. Assume further: level structures are stable under variable change, namely [`ModularCurve.IsLevelPStructure`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelP.html#L104) for $\ell$ under `LevelPData.variableChange` and [`ModularCurve.IsGamma0PowAt`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma0Pow.html#L55) under [`ModularCurve.kernelVariableChangeDeg`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassLevelComponents.html#L104), over every $A_0$-algebra; a family $\mathcal{G}$ of relative group laws on the Proj models of projective Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant over $A_0$-algebras which is chord–tangent (each group law is induced, compatibly with addition and Galois twists, by the affine group law over fields) and whose unit section is the origin chart with $x/y = z/y = 0$; a transport $\mathcal{T}$ of raw Drinfeld pairs of level $q$ along $A_0$-algebra maps and variable changes preserving Drinfeld bases, whose transported sections agree with the original ones after composition with the graded maps of Proj models; and the existence, for all projective Weierstrass curves over $A_0$-algebras, of graded homomorphisms of the homogeneous coordinate rings realising a given variable change, respectively a given coefficient change, and pulling the irrelevant ideal back appropriately. Let $P_0$ be an abstract moduli package over $A_0$ for the moduli datum of `rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ M' q`, i.e. a ring $B_0$ of finite type over $A_0$ with a universal object such that, for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, the $T$-points — Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant equipped with a $\Gamma_0$-kernel polynomial for each prime power dividing $M'$, a level-$\ell$ structure and a Drinfeld $q$-basis, taken up to variable change — are classified uniquely by $A_0$-algebra maps $B_0 \to T$, the $j$-invariant being `jOf`. Let $x$ be such a point over $K$ whose $j$-invariant has Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18). Then, for every prime ideal $\mathfrak{q}$ of $B_0$ containing the kernel of the classifying homomorphism $B_0 \to K$ attached to $x$, and every $n \in \mathbb{N}$, that kernel is contained in $\mathfrak{q}^n$.
--
--   The statement says that the kernel of the map classifying the Tate point over the unramified base $A_0$ is adically negligible at every prime containing it, the kernel being generated by differences of roots of unity of $\ell$-power order and hence by idempotents. It is used in the construction of moduli packages whose relevant stalks are identified, after adic completion, with rings of the full-level modular tower.
